# Download and scratch caches for encode-music.mjs.
#
# _wav/ is ~98 MB of source WAVs pulled from Supabase and vidIQ. It is a cache,
# not a source: every URL in it is recorded in encode-music.mjs, so it can be
# rebuilt from scratch at any time. The script deliberately does NOT delete it
# on success, because wiping it meant every adjustment to the trim or the
# crossfade cost a full re-download before you could see whether the adjustment
# worked. Delete it by hand when the music is settled.
#
# _trim/ is the intermediate between trimming and encoding and is removed
# automatically; it is listed here only so an interrupted run cannot leave it
# staged.
_wav/
_trim/

# THIS FILE LIVES HERE, NOT IN THE ROOT .gitignore, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE.
# The root .gitignore is an input to the Expo fingerprint — it appears as a
# `bareGitIgnore` source in `expo-updates fingerprint:generate`. Editing it
# changes runtimeVersion. Nested .gitignore files are not fingerprint sources.
# Same reasoning as coplas-web/.gitignore; see that file.

# Caches for optimize-video.mjs. _video_orig/ is ~1.26 GB of pristine source
# clips and is the ONLY way back if a re-encode turns out too aggressive —
# keep it until the contact sheet has been approved and the app has shipped.
# _video_uploaded.txt is the append-on-success ledger that makes an interrupted
# upload resumable rather than a redo.
_video_orig/
_video_small/
_video_uploaded.txt
video-compare.png
_scene_orig/
_scene_test/
_tier_test/
tier-compare.png
_video_settings.json
_fps_test/
crf-compare.png
